            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5",
            "treatment.6"
          ],
          "text": "ECG demonstrated T-wave inversion in V4-6 and troponin rose from 287 to 412. GRACE score was high risk. Inpatient coronary angiogram confirmed severe three-vessel coronary artery disease. Following MDT review, she was deemed not suitable for PCI and a decision was made to manage her medically. Dual antiplatelet therapy was commenced with ticagrelor, fondaparinux was started, bisoprolol was uptitrated to 7.5mg once daily, and isosorbide mononitrate 30mg once daily was added. Creatinine was 168 on Day 2 (13/05), improving to 142 by Day 4 (15/05). She mobilised with physiotherapy and a cardiac rehabilitation referral was completed. DNACPR was discussed and agreed with the patient and family; the DNACPR form was completed 14/05.",
